  "summary": "Federated learning has been applied to sepsis early warning in several recent studies. Iyer et al. used a federated approach on ICU vital signs from the IEEE-CIS dataset and reported an accuracy of 0.91 [D0063]. Brennan et al. applied federated learning to the MIMIC-IV dataset for early detection of septic deterioration, achieving a MAPE of 0.868 [D0062]. Okafor et al. evaluated privacy‑preserving training across institutions without pooling data—a federated‑style method—on the SentinelYield-2 dataset and obtained an F1 score of 0.726 [D0064]. Haddad et al. also used federated learning on the HateCheck dataset, reporting an AUROC of 0.672 [D0061]. For comparison, Brennan et al. presented a non‑federated boosted decision‑tree ensemble on MIMIC‑IV that achieved a MAPE of 0.682, illustrating the performance of traditional models on the same task [D0065].",
